<SiteLayout title="Licenses & credits" description="RepoReady's MIT license, upstream project attribution, media review boundaries, and per-app redistribution requirements." canonicalPath="/licenses/">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Open source, with attribution</p><h1>Licenses & credits</h1><p>Every project has its own license and redistribution conditions. A catalog listing does not grant additional rights to its software, models, or media.</p></header>
  <div class="prose"><h2>RepoReady</h2><p>RepoReady is licensed under the MIT License. Copyright © 2026 Pranoy Mukherjee. Read the <a href="https://github.com/Pranoym17/RepoReady/blob/main/LICENSE">full license in the source repository</a>, including its permission and warranty terms.</p><h2>Upstream projects</h2><p>Candidate detail pages identify the upstream author, source, license evidence, and unresolved review questions. Authors and contributors retain credit for their projects. Names are used to identify the projects; listing them does not imply endorsement or affiliation.</p><p>Software, bundled dependencies, model weights, datasets, and installer assets may have different license conditions. License review and required notices must be completed before a release is approved for redistribution.</p><h2>Screenshots and other media</h2><p>This initial catalog does not present candidate screenshots as reviewed assets. Draft pages label the media review gap. Approved publication requires reviewed screenshot provenance, permission or license, meaningful alternative text, and credits. No generated image is presented as an actual tested application screenshot.</p><h2>Website foundations</h2><p>The website uses <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and system fonts. Website styling and the RepoReady letter mark are defined in the project's source. Dependency license notices remain with their respective packages.</p><h2>Corrections and rights concerns</h2><p>If attribution or a license disclosure is inaccurate, follow the <a href="/support/">reporting guidance</a> and include the relevant project and source evidence.</p></div>
</SiteLayout>
